# ML Development Practices

## Framework & Architecture
- Use PyTorch as primary deep learning framework
- Custom neural architecture for educational content structure
- Specialized word embeddings trained on educational terminology
- Sequence-to-sequence modeling with attention mechanisms
- Start with baseline models before custom architectures

## Model Development Guidelines
- Separate model definition, training, and evaluation code
- Implement reproducible experiments with proper seed setting
- Log experiments with clear naming conventions
- Document hyperparameters and model architectures
- Include model versioning and checkpointing

## Training Practices
- Implement comprehensive logging (loss, metrics, hyperparameters)
- Use proper train/validation/test data handling
- Monitor for overfitting and implement early stopping
- Document training procedures and computational requirements
- Regular experimental validation and results analysis

## Experimentation Standards
- Version control all experiment configurations
- Maintain experiment logs with timestamps and results
- Compare against established baselines consistently
- Document failed experiments and lessons learned
- Iterative development with clear progression tracking

## Technical Innovation Focus
- Educational content structure understanding
- Pedagogical quality maintenance throughout generation
- Coherent course content progression modeling
